meta {
  name: 01 Go Online
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/drivers/online
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{driver_access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "lat": 5.3600,
    "lng": -4.0083
  }
}

tests {
  test("status is 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("status is online", function () {
    expect(res.body.status).to.equal("online");
  });
}

docs {
  Requires the driver's KYC to be approved (folder 03) and a vehicle registered
  (folder 02) — otherwise `403 DRIVER_NOT_VERIFIED` or `409 NO_ACTIVE_VEHICLE`
  (`app_base/modules/ride/application/driver_service.py:253-270`).

  This single REST call seeds BOTH the Redis presence marker (`drivers:seen:{id}`,
  30s TTL) and the availability marker (`drivers:available:{id}`, 300s TTL) — see
  `app_base/modules/ride/infra/driver_location.py:56-84`. No WebSocket connection is
  needed to make this driver matchable.

  **Timing**: run "06-Ride-Lifecycle / 01 Create Ride" within 30 seconds of this
  request, or the presence marker expires and the driver silently drops out of
  matching (`find_available_nearby`) even though `AVAILABLE_KEY` is still set.
}
